    "notes": "Stuart's cavalry was absent July 1-2, depriving Lee of intelligence. Stuart arrived July 2 afternoon. July 3 East Cavalry Field is the major cavalry action."
  },
  "cavalry_commander": {
    "name": "Major General J.E.B. Stuart",
    "fate": "Survived Gettysburg -- killed Yellow Tavern May 1864",
    "notes": "Stuart's controversial absence left Lee blind during the approach march. Lee reportedly greeted him with 'General Stuart, where have you been?' Stuart arrived late July 2."
  },
